body:
@janos-r Having a non-NF variant is covered by #2550.

I believe that having the Nerd Font variant as the default is the way to go: practically all the other "fancy prompt" projects use NF, a NF font is super easy to install, and it certainly looks better on screenshots.

However, I think we can both agree that "having non-NF as the default, NF optional" and "fully utilizing NF, non-NF optional" are both better variants than the current "use NF for some languages (like Node.js) while using emoji for others (like Python)", which requires NF while not taking advantage of it.
